# Epic — Pedagogical QA

> **For epic-executor:** This epic will be executed wave-by-wave.
> **Required pre-reading by every wave's build subagent:**
> 1. Charter: `automatiklabs/docs/educational-system/CHARTER.md`
> 2. Context: `docs/educational-system/context/pedagogical-qa.md`
> 3. Skill: `automatiklabs-doctrine`

## Goal

Publish the `pedagogical-gate-rubric` as a versioned YAML artifact and atomic skill, implement the `pedagogical-drift-detector` worker, and wire the 8 hard-fail criteria into `fn_validate_lesson_doctrine` — creating an automated pre-screening layer that filters ~60% of lessons before they reach the human review queue.

## Scope

- Publishes `pedagogical-gate-rubric.yaml` with exactly 8 hard-fail criteria.
- Creates the `pedagogical-gate-rubric` skill wrapping those criteria.
- Implements the `pedagogical-drift-detector` worker (Python, runs locally via Bash tool).
- Defines the JSON Schema for `pedagogical_reviews.criterion_results`.
- Does NOT write lesson content, does NOT write schema migrations (those are Schema Extensions), does NOT adjudicate content disputes.

